1
00:00:00,031 --> 00:00:03,234
Quite how they got the tickets, but they did well to do so.

2
00:00:03,616 --> 00:00:04,117
And they're here.

3
00:00:04,237 --> 00:00:11,467
We're waiting for a big step up in class from Paolo Espinoza Sanchez, bronze medalist of the World Championships last year.

4
00:00:11,506 --> 00:00:18,036
Naomi Baki of Italy, born in Hungary, but now representing Italy.

5
00:00:21,179 --> 00:00:24,064
Julia Prokopchuk of the Ukraine.

6
00:00:25,882 --> 00:00:30,647
Now the second of the Canadians, again looking for a slightly better performance.

7
00:00:30,687 --> 00:00:35,234
She'll need it if she wants to make it into the top 12, which is where we will be at the end of this session.

8
00:00:35,393 --> 00:00:38,436
And now full of beans, full of life and full of words.

9
00:00:39,679 --> 00:00:41,299
Katie Bell of the USA.

10
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:43,021
Watch her preparation for every dive.

11
00:00:43,542 --> 00:00:45,945
She'll be having a little chat or a chunter to herself.

12
00:00:49,289 --> 00:00:51,451
Mai Nagagawa of Japan.

13
00:00:53,947 --> 00:00:55,151
into the last seven.

14
00:00:55,210 --> 00:00:58,540
Now, this is the order in which they will dive five rounds of dives.

15
00:00:58,581 --> 00:01:01,530
Remember in the women's Yulia Coltanova.

16
00:01:02,152 --> 00:01:03,134
Those are the two Chinese.

17
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:05,862
It's Yabang Hu.

18
00:01:10,433 --> 00:01:13,496
Women's 10 meter platform semi-final.

19
00:01:14,138 --> 00:01:18,424
They're just introducing the 18 who made it through from an original list of 26.

20
00:01:18,463 --> 00:01:20,206
Sadie from a British point of view.

21
00:01:20,266 --> 00:01:21,989
No representation.

22
00:01:22,009 --> 00:01:23,512
Stacey Powell didn't make it through.

23
00:01:23,552 --> 00:01:25,453
Naughty Monique Gladding.

24
00:01:25,734 --> 00:01:30,200
She was 19th last night, so she missed out on that last remaining place.

25
00:01:30,221 --> 00:01:34,406
Christian Stur of Germany had an exceptional performance last night.

26
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:36,891
Leon Taylor, as ever, is alongside me.

27
00:01:36,911 --> 00:01:37,891
The 10 meter

28
00:01:38,429 --> 00:01:41,893
Synchro silver medalist from 2004 in Athens.

29
00:01:41,933 --> 00:01:45,777
I think it's safe to say Leon, the standard last night left a little bit to be desired.

30
00:01:46,236 --> 00:01:51,882
Yeah, it seemed to me that not many of these ladies wanted to make it through to this semi-final.

31
00:01:52,283 --> 00:02:02,614
But Shen Ruolin, the Olympic champion, only 15 years old, four years ago in Beijing, tops the field or top the field by a huge margin by the end of the proceedings last night.

32
00:02:02,593 --> 00:02:29,242
it's a tough program for these young ladies they are on again and they didn't finish until late last night they were still diving close to 10 pm obviously back to the olympic village have something to eat to rest try and turn your adrenaline down to get some sleep and then get back up early this morning to come in and practice your dives from the mighty 10 meter platform there towering above all the other diving boards this is the dive order once again and of course

33
00:02:29,223 --> 00:02:30,564
The girls do five dives.

34
00:02:31,066 --> 00:02:37,093
Each of those dives counts and it's the total score, which means you make it through or you don't.

35
00:02:37,153 --> 00:02:42,382
Top 12 go through to this evening's final, so it's a lot of diving in a short space of time.

36
00:02:42,802 --> 00:02:45,787
Who is the fittest and who can hold it together mentally?

37
00:02:45,866 --> 00:02:47,669
Last night, lots of faltering.

38
00:02:47,849 --> 00:02:49,192
Will we see the same this morning?

39
00:02:49,472 --> 00:02:51,314
I think we might see one or two.

40
00:02:51,294 --> 00:02:52,757
What about Monique Gladding?

41
00:02:52,918 --> 00:02:57,645
It was a surprise to some actually she even competed last night because she had a quite serious injury.

42
00:02:57,844 --> 00:02:59,147
She did, what an absolute shame.

43
00:02:59,187 --> 00:03:10,825
Monique Gladding finishing 19th, Stacey Powell 20th so they're both reserve one and reserve two but none of the ladies ahead of them have been injured in the meantime and so they're watching on the poolside thinking what if.

44
00:03:11,006 --> 00:03:17,015
Monique Gladding of course hitting her head on the diving board in Russia only just over a year ago

45
00:03:16,996 --> 00:03:24,866
And, yeah, fortunately, knocking herself out, sunk to the bottom of the pool, rescued by her teammate Nicholas Robinson Baker.

46
00:03:25,247 --> 00:03:33,437
A truly dramatic story, an inspirational story, how she came back and made the Olympic Games team at the age of 31, her first Olympic Games.

47
00:03:33,538 --> 00:03:44,872
Such a shame to see her not featuring today in the semi-final alongside Stacey Powell as well, having a tough day in the diving pool, meaning reserve one and reserve two.

48
00:03:45,174 --> 00:03:46,074
What a shame.

49
00:03:46,747 --> 00:03:51,557
Right, so just say how this works in case you're new to diving and haven't seen our coverage up to this point.

50
00:03:51,717 --> 00:03:53,301
The marks will appear on your screen.

51
00:03:53,481 --> 00:03:56,849
All the marks that have lines through them will not count towards the total.

52
00:03:56,909 --> 00:03:59,977
In other words, the top and bottom marks are discarded.

53
00:04:00,037 --> 00:04:03,405
The three in the middle will be taken as their marks.

54
00:04:03,384 --> 00:04:06,348
and they will be multiplied by the degree of difficulty.

55
00:04:06,368 --> 00:04:09,032
Now, in most cases, in the first round, it will be 3.0.

56
00:04:09,693 --> 00:04:12,396
We might go down into the twos, we do go down into the twos.

57
00:04:12,417 --> 00:04:16,242
We only go as high in the women's as opposed to the men's, Leon, as 3.3.

58
00:04:16,482 --> 00:04:17,783
Yeah, let me just explain.

59
00:04:17,803 --> 00:04:25,194
The degree of difficulty is assigned to each of the dives, and it depends on how difficult the dive is to how high the degree of difficulty is.

60
00:04:25,233 --> 00:04:31,182
And in this competition, we see ranging from 2.7 up to a highest of 3.3.

61
00:04:31,161 --> 00:04:40,516
Now I can explain that as it goes on, but what you're looking at, seven execution judges, the two highest and two lowest marks are discounted, so they have lines through them.

62
00:04:40,838 --> 00:04:45,865
This is so we average out any, well, any amount of subjectivity to leave three marks.

63
00:04:46,266 --> 00:04:52,377
Those are then, as Bob said, totaled and multiplied by the degree of difficulty to give the total for that particular dive.

64
00:04:52,357 --> 00:05:00,829
The girls this morning have to do five different dives in five different directions and they have six directions to choose from, if you will.

65
00:05:01,250 --> 00:05:03,413
Forwards, which is self-explanatory.

66
00:05:03,473 --> 00:05:05,516
Backwards, which is also self-explanatory.

67
00:05:05,576 --> 00:05:09,403
Inwards, which is where you stand backwards, spin forwards towards the diving board.

68
00:05:09,382 --> 00:05:15,670
The reverse, which is the opposite, which is where you stand forwards, jump away from the diving board and spin backwards towards it.

69
00:05:15,970 --> 00:05:19,954
And the twist group, which is where you rotate longitudinally as well.

70
00:05:20,115 --> 00:05:21,255
That's really complicated.

71
00:05:21,295 --> 00:05:26,721
And of course, the sixth group, which is available on the platform, is the handstand, the armstand group.

72
00:05:27,083 --> 00:05:28,384
And some girls choose to do that.

73
00:05:28,444 --> 00:05:36,353
And my co-commentator, Bob Ballard, gets ever so nervous when the girls or the boys do handstands from the 10 meter platform.

74
00:05:36,569 --> 00:05:42,978
Now they made it easy for you this morning in as much as the first 10 divers will all do exactly the same dive.

75
00:05:43,019 --> 00:05:48,127
So you get a chance to compare and contrast how good or bad or indifferent the dives are.

76
00:05:48,507 --> 00:05:54,738
So the first 10 all opting for a forward three and a half somersaults in the pike position.

77
00:05:55,238 --> 00:05:58,004
As you see on your screen, 3.0 degree of difficulty.

78
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:00,567
So the marks that count will be multiplied by that

79
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:02,603
for all of the first 10 divers.

80
00:06:02,843 --> 00:06:06,711
First up is Kim of the People's Republic of Korea.

81
00:06:09,458 --> 00:06:17,494
Well, she was probably one of the surprises making it through, just scraping in in 18th spot, but that's a very steady opening dive.

82
00:06:18,115 --> 00:06:18,857
What are you looking for?

83
00:06:18,877 --> 00:06:22,324
Right on the end of the diving board, do you notice a towel on the end of the diving board there?

84
00:06:22,343 --> 00:06:25,149
That's just preference for the divers.

85
00:06:25,290 --> 00:06:36,495
It is actually a non-slip surface on the platform, but some divers prefer probably from a comfort point of view to put a wet towel down to add to some grip, but that's a solid start from Kim.

86
00:06:36,475 --> 00:06:45,447
Yeah, sixty-three is a mark you will probably see quite a bit off because the judges tend to go for that mid-range seven multiplied by the degree of difficulty gives you sixty-three.

87
00:06:45,788 --> 00:06:50,574
There are a few divers who are waiting to up their game considerably and here is one of them.

88
00:06:50,814 --> 00:06:53,759
The first of the Canadians you'll see Roslyn Filion.

89
00:06:55,942 --> 00:06:57,184
Second up of eighteen.

90
00:06:57,244 --> 00:07:00,889
Remember, we reduced them to twelve for the final later today.

91
00:07:01,449 --> 00:07:02,651
Again, the four, three and a half.

92
00:07:06,141 --> 00:07:08,125
Yeah, she's a little bit off her game.

93
00:07:08,165 --> 00:07:09,447
She certainly was last night.

94
00:07:09,567 --> 00:07:17,117
This young lady won a bronze medal only last week in the synchronised 10 metre event with her partners also in this contest.

95
00:07:18,298 --> 00:07:21,463
Well, it could be doing squeezing into her pike shape a little bit more there.

96
00:07:21,483 --> 00:07:22,805
It didn't look very neat and tidy.

97
00:07:22,865 --> 00:07:24,908
She's a little bit loose as she entered the water.

98
00:07:25,309 --> 00:07:26,810
Looks a little bit tired, actually.

99
00:07:27,891 --> 00:07:28,452
There we go.

100
00:07:29,345 --> 00:07:39,384
See the divers punching a hole into the water there, spreading their hands as they go in and sucking down all the air with them to try and do their rip entry, which is a splashless entry.

101
00:07:39,404 --> 00:07:41,187
Not quite as good as the opening dive.

102
00:07:41,208 --> 00:07:44,314
61.50 for Filion.

103
00:07:44,334 --> 00:07:47,100
Now here comes Maria Curio.

104
00:07:53,019 --> 00:07:55,944
Oh, Maria not quite completing the dive.

105
00:07:56,124 --> 00:07:59,267
You can see entering short to vertical as she hits the water.

106
00:07:59,949 --> 00:08:03,553
I think she needed an 11 meter platform to make this one safely.

107
00:08:03,593 --> 00:08:05,916
This, of course, only a 10 meter platform.

108
00:08:05,937 --> 00:08:07,699
Look how low she finishes to the water.

109
00:08:08,079 --> 00:08:12,064
The water would hit her on her chest and then the top of her thighs, throwing up quite a lot of splash.

110
00:08:12,444 --> 00:08:14,447
That'll be the lowest scoring dive so far.

111
00:08:14,708 --> 00:08:15,408
Early stages.

112
00:08:16,410 --> 00:08:21,677
But for this young German diver to make it through, she would need to be at the top of her game, and that's a little bit off.

113
00:08:22,112 --> 00:08:24,295
quite a bit off unfortunately from her point of view.

114
00:08:24,396 --> 00:08:34,172
So already having to play catch up forty-nine point five zero with four and a half and five sprinkled across there and she is a way off the pace early stages.

115
00:08:34,251 --> 00:08:43,346
Now, Kim Jin Ok of People's Republic of Korea, semi-finalist in Beijing and also the last two World Championships.

116
00:08:43,365 --> 00:08:47,111
So she's emulated what she's done in her last three big meets.

117
00:08:47,773 --> 00:08:49,335
Can she go one better this time?

118
00:08:52,082 --> 00:08:53,785
Well, it's really good.

119
00:08:54,788 --> 00:08:57,532
The divers are looking to enter the water.

120
00:08:57,572 --> 00:09:02,399
Fantastic support from the teammates looking to enter the water completely vertically with no splash.

121
00:09:02,419 --> 00:09:05,384
And if you're doing that, you're going to get eights and upwards from the judges.

122
00:09:05,404 --> 00:09:09,972
I think that's the best forward three and a half we've seen this morning from Kim.

123
00:09:10,206 --> 00:09:11,509
Squeezing into the pipe shape.

124
00:09:11,548 --> 00:09:14,493
Heavily taped on her ankles and calves there.

125
00:09:14,933 --> 00:09:17,937
Lots of these divers held together by sticky tape and this is one of them.

126
00:09:18,578 --> 00:09:19,059
That's good.

127
00:09:19,581 --> 00:09:20,081
Very good.

128
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:20,982
70.50.

129
00:09:21,442 --> 00:09:24,587
A couple of eights and a 7.5 to count towards the total.

130
00:09:25,129 --> 00:09:28,573
Times three and you get the picture and you get the calculation.

131
00:09:29,434 --> 00:09:33,541
Now Brittany Viola who has a big support team including her dad.

132
00:09:34,462 --> 00:09:36,885
Who's a major league baseball legend.

133
00:09:37,827 --> 00:09:38,187
Frank.

134
00:09:39,399 --> 00:09:45,811
And the Americans going with a four, three and a half as indeed all the previous four have done.

135
00:09:49,115 --> 00:09:51,399
Yeah, just letting the dive run over.

136
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:58,692
Brittany really attacking the takeoff there, cranking up the rotation, which is well, exactly what you want to be doing.

137
00:09:59,195 --> 00:10:00,397
Have a little bit of a nap there.

138
00:10:01,317 --> 00:10:03,379
Might be a bit tired from a late finish last night.

139
00:10:03,941 --> 00:10:04,381
Here we go.

140
00:10:04,481 --> 00:10:06,203
Squeezing into the pike shape.

141
00:10:06,745 --> 00:10:07,745
All looks good so far.

142
00:10:07,865 --> 00:10:09,768
Just out a little bit late from the rotation.

143
00:10:09,807 --> 00:10:11,530
Rolls over a touch.

144
00:10:12,292 --> 00:10:15,735
Still get over 65 points which will keep her in contention.

145
00:10:15,775 --> 00:10:17,518
I'm surprised to see her this low down finish.

146
00:10:17,538 --> 00:10:20,562
She did make one mistake though last night to move her down the pack.

147
00:10:20,778 --> 00:10:22,802
Yeah, we expect her to move up as well.

148
00:10:22,822 --> 00:10:23,865
67.50.

149
00:10:24,004 --> 00:10:28,615
It's a solid opening dive for her that puts her in second place for the time being.

150
00:10:28,655 --> 00:10:35,110
Now, the big surprise to me last night was this lady, Paolo Espinosa-Sanchez.

151
00:10:35,150 --> 00:10:36,193
Bronze medalist last year.

152
00:10:36,274 --> 00:10:38,399
Never really got going in a program.

153
00:10:38,418 --> 00:10:39,782
Perhaps she will on this occasion.

154
00:10:41,618 --> 00:10:46,423
Yep, see it's still not as good as we would expect from Paola Espinosa.

155
00:10:46,942 --> 00:10:54,230
Multiple medallist at world level and of course Olympic medallist only last week in the synchronised 10 metre platform.

156
00:10:54,610 --> 00:10:59,875
Here just arching as she goes into the water giving the impression the dive is further over than it actually was.

157
00:10:59,995 --> 00:11:02,437
So over from vertical splash comes towards us there.

158
00:11:02,817 --> 00:11:07,643
She'll only get sevens on that, better than her prelim but still not as good as we expect.

159
00:11:07,623 --> 00:11:11,229
I'm going for her to come to life and show what she really is all about.

160
00:11:11,269 --> 00:11:16,840
She was so impressive last year at the Worlds, but so far we haven't seen anything like that kind of form from her.

161
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:22,028
Now the Hungarian born, Italian representing Naomi Bakke.

162
00:11:22,909 --> 00:11:23,792
Again, same dive.

163
00:11:26,775 --> 00:11:29,839
Oh, again, Naomi just letting the dive run over a vertical.

164
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:33,442
You can see the sprays there from the side of the pool.

165
00:11:33,562 --> 00:11:36,986
It's actually like a hosepipe spraying water just onto the surface.

166
00:11:37,027 --> 00:11:43,734
The reason for this is so you disturb the surface of the water so the divers can see exactly where they want to land.

167
00:11:43,994 --> 00:11:49,500
So if the water was still, you could see the bottom of the pool, which is actually 5.8 metres further away.

168
00:11:50,039 --> 00:11:55,686
So the sprays disturbing the water so the divers know exactly when to grab their hands and try and enter the water.

169
00:11:56,695 --> 00:11:58,756
She might be a bit disturbed by that score there actually.

170
00:11:58,777 --> 00:12:01,660
58.50 not quite what she would have hoped for.

171
00:12:02,201 --> 00:12:05,325
Remember it's five rounds and plenty of time for reparation.

172
00:12:06,385 --> 00:12:09,350
Iulia Rogopchuk of Ukraine.

173
00:12:10,171 --> 00:12:11,972
Right down to diver number 11.

174
00:12:11,993 --> 00:12:13,053
We'll see exactly the same.

175
00:12:13,114 --> 00:12:14,716
She's diver number six.

176
00:12:15,956 --> 00:12:18,179
And there's that four, three and a half again.

177
00:12:19,847 --> 00:12:21,530
Oh, that's very tidy.

178
00:12:21,552 --> 00:12:26,522
She needs to squeeze into her pike shape a little bit to get most marks from the judges.

179
00:12:26,562 --> 00:12:29,707
There should be no daylight in between the thighs and the chest.

180
00:12:29,727 --> 00:12:33,535
And as you can see there, you can almost drive a small car through that gap.

181
00:12:33,615 --> 00:12:39,307
It needs to be a lot tighter, but she does a very good entry on the end of the dive there.

182
00:12:40,250 --> 00:12:42,231
Yeah, it's an interesting technique.

183
00:12:42,251 --> 00:12:46,816
Normally the divers wrap around the backs of the carves with the forearms.

184
00:12:47,556 --> 00:12:49,238
Yulia there holding on with her hands.

185
00:12:49,278 --> 00:12:50,139
That's very difficult.

186
00:12:50,158 --> 00:12:53,041
You need an incredible amount of arm strength, but she gets eights on it.

187
00:12:53,221 --> 00:12:53,621
She does.

188
00:12:53,662 --> 00:12:55,143
72 puts her in the lead.

189
00:12:55,163 --> 00:12:58,826
A reminder to you, the judges do not see the replays that you see.

190
00:12:58,885 --> 00:13:02,609
They judge it purely on what they see in real time.

191
00:13:02,729 --> 00:13:09,294
So if we see anything on the replays that they don't, it will be because they only get one look and we get several.

192
00:13:09,274 --> 00:13:35,620
Megan Benfito second of the Canadians with her opening dive There you can see the difference in the pike shape there between Megan and Lulia Squeezing in so there was no daylight in between her body and her thighs look at this squeezing into that tight pike shape Completing the rotations very comfortably just letting the dive roll over as she goes in so she won't get any eight seven and a halfs I think on this one

193
00:13:37,642 --> 00:13:40,745
And I expect this lady to feature in this evening's final.

194
00:13:42,267 --> 00:13:43,688
Yeah, it'd be a big surprise if she didn't.

195
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:49,554
A lot of Canadians here to support her, both at the pool and watching on TV, I know, in the UK.

196
00:13:51,677 --> 00:13:55,522
So 7.5 has crossed the board, times three, gives you 67.50.

197
00:13:55,721 --> 00:13:58,605
Now, Katie's going to have a chat.

198
00:13:58,684 --> 00:13:59,125
Here we go.

199
00:14:00,106 --> 00:14:02,208
Preparation, has a smile, has a chat.

200
00:14:03,831 --> 00:14:04,932
She'll count herself in.

201
00:14:07,274 --> 00:14:07,894
And ready to go.

202
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,542
Oh, it seems to work though.

203
00:14:13,562 --> 00:14:15,583
She's got more moves than the chess player.

204
00:14:16,304 --> 00:14:21,251
Up there, moving around, quite nervous, talking to herself, doing what she needs to do.

205
00:14:21,831 --> 00:14:24,095
But it certainly worked for her yesterday in the prelims.

206
00:14:24,816 --> 00:14:26,217
And that's a better start here.

207
00:14:26,437 --> 00:14:29,341
Just a little bit over a vertical, but a splashless entry.

208
00:14:29,642 --> 00:14:35,830
This could get some eights from the judges and probably put her top of the leaderboard so far in this competition.

209
00:14:35,809 --> 00:14:38,274
Great start there from Katie Bell.

210
00:14:38,914 --> 00:14:39,876
I think we warmed to it.

211
00:14:40,017 --> 00:14:40,878
Certainly the crowd have.

212
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:44,203
Just for her little idiosyncrasies before she dives.

213
00:14:44,825 --> 00:14:49,011
73.50 puts Katie Bell into the lead.

214
00:14:50,794 --> 00:14:53,899
Now, my Nakagawa of Japan.

215
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:58,628
She had a very good pre-lance with a very small degree of difficulty in comparison.

216
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:00,585
Oh, now did you hear that?

217
00:15:00,644 --> 00:15:01,707
So what happened there?

218
00:15:01,727 --> 00:15:04,918
